.\" Man page for rsvptui
.TH RSVPTUI 1 "2026-06-19" "1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rsvptui \- Rapid Serial Visual Presentation terminal ebook reader
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rsvptui
.I file
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rsvptui
displays a plain text file one word at a time in the centre of the terminal,
using the RSVP technique to speed reading.  It features a modal interface with
Vim-style keys, chapter and paragraph navigation, Optimal Recognition Point
(ORP) colour highlighting, and automatic punctuation pauses.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I file
Path to a plain text file (.txt, .md, or any UTF-8 text).
.SH MODES
.B Auto mode
(default) \- words advance automatically at the configured words-per-minute
(WPM) rate.  The rate can be changed at any time with \fB+\fR/\fB\-\fR.
.P
.B Manual mode
\- words advance only when you press \fBj\fR (next) or \fBk\fR (previous).
Useful for密集 text or reference material.
.SH KEY BINDINGS
.SS Global (any mode)
.TP
\fBq\fR
Quit the program (also Ctrl+C).
.TP
\fB?\fR
Show scrollable help panel.
.TP
\fBm\fR
Toggle between Auto and Manual mode.
.TP
\fBCtrl+j\fR
Jump to next paragraph (shows overview).
.TP
\fBCtrl+k\fR
Jump to previous paragraph (shows overview).
.TP
\fB]\fR
Jump to next chapter (shows overview).
.TP
\fB[\fR
Jump to previous chapter (shows overview).
.SS Auto mode
.TP
\fB+\fR or \fBk\fR
Increase WPM by 10 (range 60-800).
.TP
\fB\-\fR or \fBj\fR
Decrease WPM by 10.
.TP
\fBSpace\fR or \fBp\fR
Pause / resume playback.
.SS Manual mode
.TP
\fBj\fR
Next word.
.TP
\fBk\fR
Previous word.
.TP
\fB+\fR
Increase WPM by 10.
.TP
\fB\-\fR
Decrease WPM by 10.
.SS Overview navigation (paragraph / chapter)
When viewing a paragraph or chapter overview:
.TP
\fBj\fR
Start reading from the first word of the selected item.
.TP
\fBk\fR
Start reading from the last word of the previous item.
.TP
\fBCtrl+j\fR / \fBCtrl+k\fR
Cycle to next / previous paragraph (paragraph overview only).
.TP
\fB]\fR / \fB[\fR
Cycle to next / previous chapter (chapter overview only).
.TP
\fBq\fR or \fBESC\fR
Exit overview without changing position.
.SS Help panel
.TP
\fBj\fR or \fBDown\fR
Scroll down.
.TP
\fBk\fR or \fBUp\fR
Scroll up.
.TP
\fBq\fR or \fBESC\fR
Close help.
.SH FEATURES
.TP
Optimal Recognition Point (ORP)
The middle letter of each word is highlighted in yellow (if the terminal
supports colour) to improve word recognition.
.TP
Punctuation pause
Words ending in \fB.\fR \fB?\fR \fB!\fR \fB:\fR \fB;\fR get a 1.5x extra
delay in auto mode, mimicking natural sentence rhythm.
.TP
Progress display
Real-time progress bar with percentage, current WPM, and estimated time
remaining (ETA).
.TP
Chapter navigation
Markdown headings (\fB# ...\fR) are detected as chapter boundaries.
An overview shows the chapter title and its first paragraph content.
.TP
Paragraph navigation
Blank-line separated paragraphs are indexed for quick jumping.
.TP
Bookmarks
Progress (position, WPM, mode) is saved to
\fB~/.config/rsvp-tui/bookmarks.json\fR on exit.  On startup, if a bookmark
exists for the same file, you are prompted to resume.  Finished books are
automatically removed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TERM
The terminal must support \fBcurses\fR.  A real TTY is required; piping
output will interfere with the resume prompt and terminal rendering.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/rsvp-tui/bookmarks.json
Bookmark data (JSON).  Created automatically on first save.
.SH BUGS
Report issues at https://github.com/duartebranco/rsvptui
.SH AUTHOR
Written by Duarte Branco.
